edby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/236282-couple-of-things-from-the-new-2014-2015-schedule#post236282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Scion advert in the new OP publishing brochure, with what looks like a new piece of art, and a couple of interesting things in the blurb for Origins, expanding on what Neall's revealed. It mentions we're going to be getting three settings with different relationships between the gods and humanity, and the first tier of supernatural Purviews, from Elementals to Therianthropes and Berserkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relationships between the gods and humanity is good to hear.<br /> <br /> Umm..is there a link? I just want to see that piece of art.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T13:43:02-07:00","id":255550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/236282-couple-of-things-from-the-new-2014-2015-schedule?p=251265#post251265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the animal-headed gods of the Pesdajet is basically divine theiranthropes. Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That will definitely be one (potentially quite fun) way of playing them, yes. Part of my goal is to not be too definitive when it comes to the origins of the entities we're calling Gods in Scions. We will definitely make mentions of what mortal cultures say are their origins, hearkening back to real-world mythology, but we're not going to lay any absolutes on them. That's for the campaign type and the one running the game to decide on, in finality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Regards,<br /> Joseph D. Carriker<br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> \u201cIn Springtime, O Dionysos, To thy holy temple come,<br /> To Elis with thy Graces, Rushing with thy bull-foot, come,<br /> Noble Bull, Noble Bull\u201d<br /> \u2015 Plutarch","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1242-jdcarriker","name":"JDCarriker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T15:27:16-07:00","id":256292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JDCarriker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/236282-couple-of-things-from-the-new-2014-2015-schedule?p=255550#post255550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That will definitely be one (potentially quite fun) way of playing them, yes. Part of my goal is to not be too definitive when it comes to the origins of the entities we're calling Gods in Scions. We will definitely make mentions of what mortal cultures say are their origins, hearkening back to real-world mythology, but we're not going to lay any absolutes on them. That's for the campaign type and the one running the game to decide on, in finality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like when systems or settings leave some built in wiggle room for the GM or players to choose the origins of that setting big players. If you are bound to the exact events of the original telling of the myth, that can sometimes throw up some roadblocks to putting your own spin on things.<br /> <br /> Actually two narratives that do this very well are the comic series &quot;Fables&quot; and the TV show &quot;Once Upon a Time&quot; both re-imaginings of the classic fairy tales. The characters in both series tend to have lived the most iconic parts of their stories, but the writers take the opportunity to have different beginnings, endings, or context in the way these classic stories relate to the rest of the world,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}